1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,217
You're on hold.

2
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:07,513
That tune has a birthday.

3
00:00:08,210 --> 00:00:09,856
Nineteen sixty-two.

4
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:14,359
Alfred Levy runs a factory. And his phones have a problem.

5
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:17,291
A loose wire is touching a steel beam.

6
00:00:17,690 --> 00:00:20,472
The whole building becomes a radio antenna.

7
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:24,446
So anyone put on hold... hears a radio station.

8
00:00:24,950 --> 00:00:26,535
And they stop hanging up.

9
00:00:27,130 --> 00:00:30,300
Nobody waited less. They just stopped noticing.

10
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:33,269
Levy patents it. Music on hold.

11
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:38,015
Sixty years later, it plays on every support line on earth.

12
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:39,999
What did it fix?

13
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:41,728
Nothing.

14
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:45,788
The trick: fill the silence. People stay to be polite.

15
00:00:46,490 --> 00:00:48,094
Then, the second trick.

16
00:00:48,490 --> 00:00:51,175
A voice. “Your call is important to us.”

17
00:00:51,570 --> 00:00:53,758
Said to everyone. By no one.

18
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:56,698
Important just means: keep waiting.

19
00:00:57,400 --> 00:01:00,918
A tune nobody chose. A line nobody means.

20
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:06,904
This video opened the same way. Four seconds of hold music. No words.

21
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:08,538
You stayed.

22
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:10,837
So here's your exit.

23
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:13,505
Rasolv doesn't put you on hold.

24
00:01:13,810 --> 00:01:18,607
A real expert is already on it. Live updates. Answers in minutes.

25
00:01:19,310 --> 00:01:22,218
Which one gets you? The tune... or the answer?

26
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:25,051
Rasolv. Vision that solves.
